      "claim": "Caffeine is a central nervous system stimulant that antagonizes adenosine receptors, increasing alertness.",
      "evidence": "Pharmacology textbooks and peer‑reviewed reviews describe caffeine’s primary mechanism as adenosine‑receptor antagonism.",
